    sound // thinking about build-in tiny synthesizer code, and in game sounds are just recipes to generate sounds thru synth engine. very basic sine/tri/square/noise with fm capabilities. everything from menu clicks to sound of trees breaking apart is all synthesized. this means we could do procgen music too, set a mode and key and just let it generate ambient music/sounds

// physics/mechanics

scoop // basic unarmed left mouse button move. removes voxel material from whatever is in range and aimed at. can break stuff like trees. picks up items
chup // basic unarmed right mouse button move. karate chop stuff. cuts ropes, tree trunks (takes many hits without a tool)4
items can be thrown when held  // e.g. a shovel is thrown like a spear and sticks into a wooden board, but bounces off stone etc. 
shirt represents player health // turns to rags lower hp you get

objects have health and can be repaired/healed // e.g. a pumpkin is thrown, but doesnt break the first time just takes x damage (based on mass, velocity, and what it hit). a wood 2x4 same thing, but if you swing a hammer at it you can repair it

building system // (probably snapping to angles, 45/90/180 etc). need to determine how "welding" (to use the gmod term) objects. maybe nails and then later an actual welder to make a strong bond with metal objects

trees // trees are procgen and comprised of 2 sections, trunks and branches. branches are just bunches of green voxels, spawns sticks when destroyed or scooped. sticks can be lit on fire or built with. trunks, when broken, have the rest of the trunk fall over using the physics engine (which means it can break other stuff) further processing of trunks becomes logs, which can be turned into boards/planks/beams etc


